tive and I am interested to see how  it comes about or like are we going to  get those gadgets progressively through  the story are we gonna have them all  that's taught I'll be going to have an  upgrade system like old from everything  that we've seen I just want to know how  it walks I want to see that stuff in  action and the sort of RPG ish elements  are really interesting to me another  thing that I think is very similar to  Ockham is the enemy types whose enemy  that had a Taser some regular guys who  didn't really have much and then a guy  who had a gun and the enemy variety for  just regular kind of drone dudes like  not bosses obviously which I sure will  be very different seem very very similar  to the optin games which is of course  very similar to a hundred other games  because that's the way action-adventure  did that's the way these kind of games  watch and then aside from that the only  thing that I'm like getting big  Salieri's from but I'm kind of  interested in is how all these villains  are going to type together I mentioned  this at the start that I actually quite  liked arkham origins it was buggy and it  crashed on me and it didn't change quite  enough about the series but i enjoyed  the story as a huge DC fan who likes a  lot of those villains i'm also a fairly  big spider-man fan and i like a lot of  the villains that we've seen shown up  there way more than i expected so I'm  kind of wondering if the story is going  to be still on origins where basically  one of those villains is sort of put a  hit on Spidey and has made it so  everyone else is trying to get at him  I'm very interested to see how that  turns out and having played previous  spider-man games the one thing that I  really don't know about that I'm really  interested in is what you can do when  you're not going through story stuff  like I did do some sidequest stuff in my  time playing and there's like you know  basic go here and fight some guys but I  mean like can I do like pho